# Slack & email notification policy

## No blanket restriction

There is **no** blanket restriction on sending Slack messages or emails.

## Default (all recipients)

Before sending **any** Slack message or email, **ask the user for confirmation
first**, OR send when the user **explicitly tells you to** send it.

## STANDING EXCEPTION — dashy data refresh notification (recurring)

After **EVERY** dashy Salesforce/Databricks data refresh **+ deploy** completes
successfully, **automatically notify Bianca Medrea on Slack DM only** that the
refresh is done and to check the data. This is standing, pre-authorized: **no
per-message confirmation needed**.

> **Slack only** (updated 2026-07-09): do **not** send the recurring data-refresh
> notification by email anymore — Slack DM is the sole channel for this standing
> notification.

**Bianca Medrea** — Slack user `U01AHG4UAPR` (email `bianca.medrea@bolt.eu` kept
for reference / explicit one-off requests only).

Bianca is otherwise **pre-authorized**: when the user asks to send something to
Bianca, send directly without per-message confirmation.

### Message template

- **Slack DM:** run `node scripts/refresh-snapshot.mjs` after `npm run build` and
  send its output verbatim. It renders the greeting plus a **snapshot of the
  update** (added 2026-10-05) from the freshly built `data/dashboard.json`:

  ```
  Hi Bianca — dashy data refresh is done ✅ Latest SF + Databricks data is live on dashy.boltable.eu (updated <updatedAt>). Please check the data when you get a chance.

  *Snapshot of this update*
  *YTD:* Won … · Activated …
  *<Month> MTD (team):* Won … · Activated … · Leads … · Qualified …
  *<Prior month> (closed):* Won … · Activated …
  *Inbound MTD:* Won … · Activated …
  *Week W..:* Leads … · Qualified … · Negotiations … · Closed Won … · Active …
  *Accounts performance:* … roster accounts · GMV €… · … orders
  *Churn watch:* … problem status · … never ordered
  *MOPS:* … open cases (… onboarding) · … ready to activate
  *My Pipeline:* … open opps · … open leads
  ```

  The snapshot shows **actuals only** — targets are omitted because
  `dashboard.json` holds segment defaults while the live site applies
  `data/target-config.json` overrides at runtime.

> Sends to **other** recipients still require asking the user first or an
> explicit instruction.
